# .cursorrules — Worktime Tracker
# AI agent constraints for Cursor, Claude, GitHub Copilot
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════

## MANDATORY RULES (never violate)

### Architecture
- NEVER use external databases (PostgreSQL, MongoDB, Redis, SQLite, etc.)
- NEVER use external HTTP APIs or third-party services
- ALL persistence must be In-Memory using Map/Array collections
- ALL storage implementations must extend an Interface (IEmployeeRepository, ITimeEntryRepository, ILeaveRepository)
- NEVER add runtime dependencies to package.json (devDependencies only for jest, jest-junit)

### Interfaces & Contracts
- NEVER generate a concrete class without a corresponding Interface (I-prefixed)
- Interfaces live in src/storage/ (repositories) or src/services/ (strategies)
- Every interface method must throw new Error('Not implemented')

### Testing (TDD)
- NEVER generate business logic without accompanying tests
- Tests MUST go in tests/unit/ or tests/integration/
- Each test file must have at minimum 10 test cases
- Use jest.fn() for mocks — NEVER use sinon or other mock libraries
- Coverage target: minimum 70% lines, branches, functions, statements

### Code Quality
- ALWAYS use 'use strict' at the top of every file
- ALWAYS add JSDoc comments to public methods and classes
- NEVER use var — use const or let only
- ALWAYS validate inputs using src/utils/validators.js
- NEVER throw generic Error for validation — always throw TypeError with a descriptive message

### Design Patterns (GoF — minimum 2 required)
- Strategy pattern: OvertimeStrategy (StandardOvertimeStrategy, DoubleTimeOvertimeStrategy, TieredOvertimeStrategy, CompTimeOvertimeStrategy)
- Observer pattern: EventEmitter — EmployeeService and TimeTrackingService extend it and emit domain events

### SOLID Principles
- S — Single Responsibility: each class has one reason to change
- O — Open/Closed: extend via new Strategy implementations, not by modifying existing ones
- L — Liskov: all repository implementations are interchangeable with their interfaces
- I — Interface Segregation: keep interfaces small and focused
- D — Dependency Inversion: services receive repositories via constructor injection

### File Structure (do not deviate)
src/models/        → Domain entities (Employee, TimeEntry, Leave)
src/services/      → Business logic (EmployeeService, TimeTrackingService, LeaveService, ReportService, OvertimeStrategy)
src/storage/       → Interfaces + InMemory implementations
src/utils/         → Pure helpers (validators, dateUtils, idGenerator, EventEmitter)
tests/unit/        → Unit tests (one file per module)
tests/integration/ → Integration / scenario tests
docs/diagrams/     → UML diagrams (Mermaid .md files)
.cursor/rules/     → AI context files

### Forbidden
- NO express, fastify, koa or any HTTP framework
- NO moment.js, dayjs, date-fns or any date library (use src/utils/dateUtils.js)
- NO lodash, ramda or utility libraries
- NO class-validator, joi, yup (use src/utils/validators.js)
- NO uuid library (use src/utils/idGenerator.js)
